        "original_id": "3a80acf1-d3eb-5076-85e8-abe2496345be",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Crescograph\n- People: Sir Jagadish Chandra Bose\n- Concepts: Plant growth measurement\n- Roles: Physicist, biologist, biophysicist, botanist, archaeologist, science fiction writer\n\nFacts:\n- Sir Jagadish Chandra Bose was born on 30 November 1858 and died on 23 November 1937.\n- Sir Jagadish Chandra Bose was a Bengali polymath, physicist, biologist, biophysicist, botanist, archaeologist, and an early writer of science fiction.\n- In the early 20th century, Sir Jagadish Chandra Bose invented the crescograph.\n- A crescograph is a device used to measure growth in plants.",
